        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Tomb of Tutankhamun</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Period</span><span class="info-stat-val">c. 1323 BCE – present</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Made by</span><span class="info-stat-val">Commissioned for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tutankhamun">Tutankhamun</a>, an <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eighteenth-dynasty-of-egypt">Eighteenth Dynasty</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pharaoh">pharaoh</a> who reigned c. 1332–1323 BCE; probably begun as a non-royal tomb, possibly intended for his advisor Ay, and enlarged after the king's premature death</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Form</span><span class="info-stat-val">A rock-cut tomb of four chambers (antechamber, annexe, burial chamber and treasury) with an entrance staircase of sixteen steps and a corridor 8 metres long; painted decoration only in the burial chamber</span></div>
